[{"text": "Sample Gym Equipment Maintenance & Safety Manual 1. Equipment Identification Model Name & Number: ProRun X200 Commercial Treadmill Specifications: \u007f Dimensions: 210 x 90 x 150 cm \u007f Max User Weight: 160 kg \u007f Power Requirement: 220\u2013240V, 50Hz 2. Maintenance Procedures Routine Maintenance Schedule: \u007f Daily: Wipe console and handrails after use. \u007f Weekly: Lubricate running deck and inspect belt tension. \u007f Monthly: Check motor brushes, bolts, and electrical connections. Cleaning Instructions: Use a soft cloth with mild detergent. Avoid alcohol, ammonia, or abrasive cleaners. Part Replacements: \u007f Running Belt: Replace every 18\u201324 months depending on usage. \u007f Drive Belt: Inspect quarterly and replace if frayed. 3. Troubleshooting Guide Error Codes: \u007f E01 \u2013 Motor overload detected. \u007f E05 \u2013 Speed sensor malfunction. Common Issues & Solutions: \u007f Belt Slipping: Tighten rear roller bolts evenly. \u007f Console Not Powering On: Check power cable and fuse. 4. Safety & Usage Operational Instructions: Adjust belt speed gradually. Always attach the safety key before use. Safety Warnings: \u007f Do not use if power cable is damaged. \u007f Keep children away from moving parts. \u007f Stop immediately if unusual noise or vibration occurs.", "embedding": [-0.024605363607406616, 0.053006164729595184, 0.03753845393657684, -0.05823139473795891, -0.04065798968076706, 0.02003004029393196, -0.0002335592289455235, 0.017391430214047432, 0.03863029181957245, 0.01506477314978838, 0.014193902723491192, -0.035276785492897034, 0.030233532190322876, 0.0020910659804940224, 0.027711903676390648, 0.0025265016593039036, -0.01321254763752222, 0.01818431168794632, -0.0035354774445295334, 0.021459829062223434, 0.0627027302980423, 0.04403749108314514, -0.0141289122402668, 0.006661515682935715, 0.01672852784395218, 0.015727676451206207, 0.0425037182867527, -0.02971360832452774, 0.04388151317834854, -0.03350904956459999, -0.